--- !u!114 &191360431
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 191360429}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.TextMeshPro::TMPro.TextMeshProUGUI
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 0
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '<b>Goal</b>

    Keep the gate standing. The run ends when the gate or
    you (the Gatekeeper) fall.


    <b>Every wave has 4 steps</b>

    1. <b>Build</b> 
    Press 1, 2 or 3 to pick Archer, Cannon or Frost. Left click a spot to place it,
    right click to remove it. Enter when ready. Archer reaches far but reloads slowly,
    Cannon is in between, Frost is short range and fires fast.

    2. <b>Weapon</b> 
    Press 1 Bow (long range), 2 Sword (wide swing) or 3 Spear (long poke).

    3.
    <b>Fight</b>  WASD to move, Space or J to attack. Attacks aim at the nearest
    enemy. The bar under you fills while your weapon reloads.

    4. <b>War report</b> 
    See what the enemy sent and how it went. Enter for the next wave.


    <b>The
    War Council</b>

    The enemy is led by the War Council. Each wave it picks
    1 of 16 attack plans: an army (Grunts, Runners, Shields or Flyers) and where
    to send it (left, middle, right or all lanes). The banner at the start of the
    wave tells you what is coming, so change your defence to match.'
